course: dictionary
lesson: 12584
title: Dipped: in, down, or angled
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Dip is a short word with several uses, and dipped is one of its forms. Dipped is the past tense of dip, so it tells us something has already happened. The words around it are the clues, so read those first.
explain: «She dipped a biscuit in her milk.» Here dipped means she put the biscuit into the milk and took it out quickly. «The temperature dipped below zero overnight.» Here dipped means went down a little. The clue is temperature, which can go up or down.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. "She put a biscuit into her milk" still makes sense, so the meaning is right. Dipped can also be an adjective, as in dipped headlights, which are car lights angled down.
fact: Dip, dips, dipped and dipping are all forms of the same verb.
fact: «Dipped» means put something into a liquid and take it out quickly.
fact: «Dipped» can also mean went down a little, as in «The temperature dipped».
fact: «Dipped headlights» are car lights angled down.
fact: On a maths graph, «The line dipped in June» means the value went down for a while.
exercise: «She dipped a biscuit in her milk.» What does dipped mean here? | Broke into small pieces | Left to dry | Went up into the air | *Put into a liquid and took out quickly
exercise: «The temperature dipped below zero overnight.» What does dipped mean here? | Shook from the cold | Was painted bright blue | Went up a lot | *Went down a little
exercise: «He dipped his brush in the blue paint.» Find and copy the word that is a form of dip. | brush | paint | *dipped | blue
test: «Dad dipped the headlights as the car came towards us.» What does dipped headlights mean? | Lights that are turned off completely | *Car lights angled down | Lights that flash very fast | Lights made of glass
test: «The line on the graph dipped sharply in June.» What does dipped mean here? | Stayed perfectly flat | *Went down | Turned into a circle | Went up very high
exam: Which sentence uses dipped to mean went down a little? | «She dipped her toe in the lake.» | «He dipped his pen in the ink.» | «He dipped the bread in the soup.» | *«The river dipped gently after the rain.»
